From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:46:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: repair a sealed database whose rows refer to each other

The repair of places failed, FOREIGN KEY constraint failed: this
SQLite turns foreign keys on, and the recovery's pragma to turn them
off comes inside its transaction, where SQLite ignores it, while it
writes rows ahead of those they refer to. The repaired database's
foreign keys are now off for the copy, and the rows left referring to
a row lost with the damaged pages are dropped and counted: a visit
without its page, a bookmark without its folder. places and the prompt
carry the count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
